{"_note": "feature lines traced on the 1280-px photos (ref/list.json), read off zoomed grid panels (tools/panel.py); k13's too (panels at 2.1x and 2.3x). Keys ending _L / _R are the car's left / right. hl = the head lamp's lens; curtain = the air curtain's slot at the bumper's corner; intake = the lower intake's black, half (centre top -> outer -> centre bottom); arch / bar = the body-coloured frame inside it; hood = the bonnet's front shut line (centre -> out); tl = the tail band, half (centre top -> outer tip -> centre bottom; point 5 is the kink where the end lobe begins); valance / insert / reflector = the black lower bumper, the body-coloured panel in it, the red reflector; boot = the boot lid's lower shut line (out -> centre); blade = the black blade behind the front wheel; handles, door lines, the charge port's lid, the rear bumper's vent. tools/trace3d.py -> tools/mkdata.py -> su7_data.py. (k07 is a mirrored picture: its lettering reads backwards; its lit band shows the lamp's light line.) The rear's sections are k21's (the car's right side, read off a 2.5x panel): valance, insert (the body-coloured arch in it), recess (the black inside the arch), reflector, vent, boot (the lid's lower shut line, out -> centre), bootside (the lid's edge above the band), letters, model, plate; k32's are kept but not used (its camera is weak). The head lamp is k12's (a 6x panel): hl_L the lens, hlu_L the four lens units' middles (upper inner, upper outer, lower inner, lower outer), hlg_L the light guide (outer -> inner tip), hls1_L / hls2_L the bright lines (the hook at the outer top; the strip down the outer side and along the bottom); k68's hl is kept for the gate. The front bumper is k12's too: curtain_L, intake_L (half: centre top -> outer -> centre bottom), arch_L (the body-coloured C in the intake, along its middle: inner top -> outer -> bottom -> the hook), plate, badge; k68's curtain / intake / arch / bar are kept but not used, its hood line is. The bonnet's shut line is k00's (hood_L: from the cowl along the left wing's crown and round the front to the centre line, a 2.6x panel); k68's is kept but not used.",
